BlastEm Fedora 1.0.0 source
==========================

The RPM source archive is generated from the upstream v1.0.0 release commit:

    c258a70cb7efd722077af1a47a9fd1d05f0635a6

The rpm-builder profile uses its git_archive strategy, with this archive name
and top-level prefix:

    blastem-1.0.0.tar.gz
    blastem-1.0.0/

Equivalent source content can be produced from a clean clone with:

    git archive --format=tar.gz \
        --prefix=blastem-1.0.0/ \
        --output=blastem-1.0.0.tar.gz \
        c258a70cb7efd722077af1a47a9fd1d05f0635a6

No moving branch name is used as source input. Packaging files are staged from
the fedora/44 branch separately and are not included in the upstream archive.

The archive generated with Git 2.51.0 during packaging validation had this
SHA-256 digest:

    e9a526473e1c49f00448c93f16c61146b919ca40cdf21791b092710367b93798

The digest records the validated archive. Git's archive and compression
implementations are part of the source-generation environment, so the pinned
commit and prefix above remain the authoritative content identity.
